<title>RUSSIA: Russia to auction 13 trln rbls in T-bills Mar 12.</title>
<headline>Russia to auction 13 trln rbls in T-bills Mar 12.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will auction nine trillion roubles in 357-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 23003) and four trillion roubles in 168-day T-bills (series 22071) on March 12, the Central Bank said on Wednesday. Full details of the auctions follow:  </p>
<p>Full details of the 357-day T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		   23003</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    9.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor			     357 days</p>
<p>    Issue date			March 12, 1997</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   March 4, 1998</p>
<p>Full details of the 168-day T-bill auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		   22071</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    4.00 trln</p>
<p>    Denominations		   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor			     168 days</p>
<p>    Issue date			March 12, 1997</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   August 27, 1997</p>
<p>On March 5 the Finance Ministry will also repay about 375.58 billion roubles in interest on OFZ interest-bearing bonds (series 24007) and pay 6.92 trillion roubles in maturing six-month T-bills (series 22056).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
